    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, traced through the code as it currently stands. Two controllers map this path: `IdempotentOwnerController` matches **only** when an `Idempotency-Key` header is present; otherwise `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` handles it. Both run the same core logic (the idempotent one delegates to the other).\n\n## 1. Security gate\n- `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n\n## 2. Bean Validation on the request body (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`)\nRuns before the method body; any failure \u2192 **400**:\n- `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 2 space/`'`/`-` separated parts)\n- `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (as above, optional trailing `.`)\n- `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` (must contain non-whitespace)\n- `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern(\"^[+()\\\\d\\\\s-]+$\")`\n- `title` \u2014 optional, `@Size(1..10)`\n- `address` / `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` \u2014 optional, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern` (non-blank)\n- `email` \u2014 optional, `@Email`, `@Size(max 255)`\n- `postcode` \u2014 optional, `@Pattern(\"^\\\\d{4}$\")`\n- `registrationDate` / `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` `LocalDate`\n\n## 3. Idempotency replay (only on the `Idempotency-Key` path)\n- If the key was already seen, the previously created owner is returned as **200 OK** and *everything below is skipped*. Otherwise it delegates to the normal create.\n\n## 4. DTO \u2192 Owner mapping (`ownerMapper.toOwner`) \u2014 validations + transforms\nExecuted in this generated order; each validator throws `IllegalArgumentException` \u2192 **400**:\n1. **telephone** `normalizeTelephone`: strip non-digits, keep `+`/country code or default `+61` (dropping a leading national `0`); require 8\u201315 digits; then `E164NationalLength.check` (`+61` needs 9 national digits, `+1` needs 10).\n2. **firstName** \u2014 `normalizeLine` \u2192 `AddressNormalizer.normalize` (trim, collapse whitespace, **UPPERCASE**, expand ST/RD/AVE, reject blank).\n3. **lastName** \u2014 same normalization.\n4. **title** \u2014 same normalization (null if blank).\n5. **city** \u2014 same normalization.\n6. **birthDate** \u2014 copied as-is.\n7. **address** `composeAddress`: prefer `addressLine1` (+ `addressLine2`) normalized, else the flat `address` normalized; blank-after-normalize is rejected.\n8. **addressLine1** / **addressLine2** \u2014 `normalizeLine` (null if blank).\n9. **postcode** `PostcodeValidator.validate(city, postcode)`: must fall in the city region's range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; UNKNOWN region accepts any).\n10. **registrationDate** `RegistrationDateValidator.validate`: reject a future date. Then `Owner.setRegistrationDate` **defaults null \u2192 today** and rolls forward onto a business day (`BusinessDay.adjust`, skipping weekends/holidays).\n11. **email** `DisposableEmailDomain.validate`: reject blocklisted domains (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail). Then `Owner.setEmail` **lower-cases** it.\n12. **salutation** `composeSalutation`: `title + \" \" + lastName` (or just lastName), from the *raw* fields (original casing).\n13. `deleted` defaults to `false`.\n\n## 5. Load existing owners\n- `clinicService.findAllOwners()` \u2014 snapshot used by all checks below.\n\n## 6. Rate/capacity & duplicate guards (in this order)\n1. `DailyRegistrationLimit.isReached` \u2014 \u2265100 owners already share today's (business-day-adjusted) registration date \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n2. `IdentityKey.isDuplicate` (same telephone **and** same email among non-deleted owners) **OR** `HouseholdMatcher.isHouseholdDuplicate` (same household = normalized lastName + postcode, among non-deleted, *unless* `sharesHousehold=true`) \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n3. `CityCapacity.isFull` \u2014 \u226550 owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409 Conflict**.\n\n## 7. Derived-field side-effects set on the owner\n- `namesakeCount` = `NamesakeCounter.count` (same first+last name, case-insensitive)\n- `customerCode` = `CustomerCodeGenerator.generate` (`<REGION>-<HASH8>`, de-duplicated with a `-2`, `-3`\u2026 suffix against existing codes)\n- `bulkSignupWarning` = `BulkSignupWarning.isTriggered` (>80 owners share today's date)\n- `householdSize` = `HouseholdMatcher.householdSize`\n- `possibleDuplicateOf` = `HouseholdMatcher.possibleDuplicateOf` (null when `sharesHousehold=true`)\n\n## 8. Persist\n- `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.\n\n## 9. Post-persist side-effects\n- **Audit log**: `AUDIT.info(\"owner created id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026 membershipNumber=\u2026\")`.\n- Map to `OwnerDto` (this computes read-only derived fields: `selfLink`, `displayName`, `initials`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, `membershipPoints/Level`, `locality`, `timezone`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`, `telephoneDisplay`).\n- Set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 Created**.\n- **(Idempotent path only)** cache the returned `OwnerDto` under the `Idempotency-Key` for future replays.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging since they're easy to miss: the name fields are silently **upper-cased** by the address normalizer (reused via `normalizeLine`), and the E.164/postcode/email/registration-date validators live *inside the mapper*, so they surface as generic `IllegalArgumentException`s (400) rather than as Bean Validation errors."
